Description: EGL takes zink through DRI3, not kopper, while the compositor announces stereo
 Kopper, zink's own window system path, has no second view of a window: an EGL
 two-view window surface on zink (NVIDIA's Vulkan driver) showed the left view
 in both eyes unless LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE=1 was set for the program. The EGL X11
 platform decides as GLX does since patch 0029: LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE set to 0 or 1
 decides as before; unset it is no while the root window announces
 _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_SUPPORTED 2 or newer and DRI3 is connected. The route
 is named in the log (EGL_LOG_LEVEL=info).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_x11.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_x11.c
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
 #include "util/bitscan.h"
 #include "util/macros.h"
 #include "util/u_debug.h"
+#include "util/os_misc.h"
 #include "util/log.h"
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
@@ -1426,12 +1427,14 @@
       return EGL_FALSE;
 #endif
 
+   bool dri3_connected = false;
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBDRM
    /* If LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2 is enabled, skip the X11 render device checks.
     * We're going to enable Zink anyway.
     */
    if (!force_zink) {
       bool status = dri3_x11_connect(dri2_dpy, disp->Options.ForceSoftware);
+      dri3_connected = status;
       /* the status here is ignored for zink-with-kopper and swrast,
        * otherwise return whatever error/fallback status as failure
        */
@@ -1442,6 +1445,20 @@
 
    dri2_detect_swrast_kopper(disp);
 
+   /* Kopper, zink's own window system path, has no second view of a window:
+    * while the compositor announces stereo content (declaration version 2 or
+    * later) zink goes through DRI3, as GLX does. LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE set to 0
+    * or 1 decides as before. */
+   if (dri2_dpy->kopper && dri3_connected && !os_get_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE") &&
+       dri2_x11_stereo_support_version(dri2_dpy) >= 2) {
+      _eglLog(_EGL_INFO, "zink through DRI3, not kopper: the compositor announces stereo content "
+                         "and kopper has no second view of a window");
+      dri2_dpy->kopper = false;
+      dri2_dpy->swrast = (disp->Options.ForceSoftware && strcmp(dri2_dpy->driver_name, "vmwgfx")) ||
+                         !dri2_dpy->driver_name || strstr(dri2_dpy->driver_name, "swrast");
+      dri2_dpy->swrast_not_kms = dri2_dpy->swrast && (!dri2_dpy->driver_name || strcmp(dri2_dpy->driver_name, "kms_swrast"));
+   }
+
    if (dri2_dpy->kopper)
       return dri2_initialize_x11_kopper(disp, force_zink);
 
